          "text": "The pattern indexes as a body-centered tetragonal cell with \\(a \\approx 6.3383\\) \u00c5 and \\(c \\approx 7.4010\\) \u00c5. The systematic absences and peak sequence are consistent with **I4/mcm (No. 140)** and the tetragonal alkali-cyanate/thiocyanate structure type. The OCN group is represented by the centrosymmetric, head\u2013tail-disordered average structure; Cu X-ray data dominated by Tl cannot reliably distinguish O from N occupational ordering.\n\n### Primary CIF\n\n```cif\ndata_TlOCN_tetragonal_average\n\n_audit_creation_method                 'indexed and structure-modelled from supplied Cu Kalpha1 powder pattern'\n_chemical_name_common                  'thallium(I) cyanate'\n_chemical_formula_structural           'Tl(OCN)'\n_chemical_formula_sum                  'Tl C N O'\n_cell_formula_units_Z                  4\n\n_cell_length_a                         6.3383(8)\n_cell_length_b                         6.3383(8)\n_cell_length_c                         7.4010(12)\n_cell_angle_alpha                      90\n_cell_angle_beta                       90\n_cell_angle_gamma                      90\n_cell_volume                           297.33(10)\n\n_space_group_crystal_system            tetragonal\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt              'I 4/m c m'\n_space_group_IT_number                 140\n\n_exptl_crystal_density_diffrn          5.505\n_diffrn_radiation_type                 'Cu Kalpha1'\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength           1.5406\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_Wyckoff_symbol\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\n_atom_site_U_iso_or_equiv\nTl1  Tl  a  0.00000  0.00000  0.25000  1.000  0.012\nC1   C   d  0.00000  0.50000  0.00000  1.000  0.020\nO1   O   h  0.1330   0.6330   0.00000  0.500  0.030\nN1   N   h  0.1330   0.6330   0.00000  0.500  0.030\n```\n\nThe terminal-site coordinate gives an average C\u2013(O,N) distance of about 1.19 \u00c5. O and N share the 8h site with 0.5 occupancy, representing head\u2013tail disorder of the linear cyanate ion.\n\nRepresentative indexing:\n\n| hkl | Calculated 2\u03b8 (\u00b0) | Observed 2\u03b8 (\u00b0) |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| 110 | 19.79 | 19.79 |\n| 002 | 24.03 | 24.03 |\n| 200 | 28.14 | 28.13 |\n| 112 | 31.32 | 31.32 |\n| 211 | 33.83 | 33.82 |\n| 202 | 37.33 | 37.33 |\n| 220 | 40.21 | 40.21 |\n| 310 | 45.17 | 45.18\u201345.23 |\n| 222 | 47.39 | 47.39 |\n| 004 | 49.19 | 49.19 |\n| 312 | 51.84 | 51.82 |\n| 321 | 53.53 | 53.53 |\n| 204 | 57.64 | 57.63 |\n| 400 | 58.17 | 58.1\u201358.2 |\n| 330 | 62.08 | 62.08 |\n| 402 | 63.86 | 63.8\u201363.9 |\n| 224 | 65.35 | 65.34 |\n| 420 | 65.86 | 65.82 |\n| 332 | 67.56 | 67.56 |\n| 314 | 69.02 | 69.01 |\n| 422 | 71.18 | 71.17\u201371.22 |\n\nAn ordered assignment of O and N would require a lower-symmetry superstructure or complementary neutron/single-crystal data; it is not uniquely supported by this powder pattern.",
